From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:53:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: generate the full 7.1 legacy AIDL surface, and verify
 it on the wire

All fourteen legacy interfaces now exist, generated from the stock 7.1 binary rather than typed:
IImsCallSession (28), IImsCallSessionListener (30), IImsUt (18), IImsVideoCallProvider (11),
IImsRegistrationListener (11), IImsConfig (9), IImsUtListener (7), IImsVideoCallCallback (7),
ImsConfigListener (4), IImsService (16), and the four two-method ones. 148 transactions.

Hand-transcribing that many signatures is where a silent, hardware-only failure comes from, so
gen-legacy-aidl.py reads method order from each $Stub's TRANSACTION_ constants and signatures from
the interface's descriptors. verify-legacy-aidl.sh then checks the BUILT apk -- not the .aidl source
-- against the stock binary: all 14 match on every transaction code and descriptor. The verifier is
negative-tested; corrupting one code fails it.

Also adds the remaining four parcelables. Their wire order is not their declaration order --
ImsCallForwardInfo writes condition, status, toA, number, timeSeconds, serviceClass -- and
ImsConferenceState marshals a map as size then String/Bundle pairs.

aidl/android/view/Surface.aidl declares a framework parcelable that has no .aidl of its own; the
platform resolves it through framework.aidl, which a device module does not get.
